    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Full suite is green (25 tests, 0 failures). Change is complete.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `membershipTier` is a derived, read-only field, so I implemented it the same way the existing derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`) are \u2014 at response-mapping time, no persistence.\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0\n       && owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank()\n       ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\"\n   ```\n   `namesakeCount == 0` and a present email \u2192 `SILVER`; otherwise `BRONZE`. Null-guards keep it safe even if `namesakeCount` or `email` are unset.\n\nBoth new Cp15 tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) pass, and all 25 tests remain green.",
